We have to work&nbsp;on the sides now.

00:28:50.600 --> 00:28:55.270
For that, we're going to use, what they call, hay chips.

00:28:55.270 --> 00:29:01.980
It's like&nbsp;this slice of the haybale straight, 
and we put it on the sides.

00:29:16.754 --> 00:29:18.235
- Yummy...

00:29:18.660 --> 00:29:20.000
Poo Palace!

00:29:21.440 --> 00:29:23.103
But, what does that mean

00:29:23.720 --> 00:29:29.554
After this first try, we realized that we need some lids,
 to keep the&nbsp;buckets closed and avoid the smell.

00:29:31.500 --> 00:29:35.760
We're just gonna make some very simple wooden lids,
to keep the smelling and animals out.

00:29:50.908 --> 00:29:52.477
So, we have our first lid!

00:29:52.477 --> 00:29:55.342
It is held together&nbsp;by two supports on the bottom.

00:29:55.342 --> 00:29:58.188
It fits into the bucket, which prevents it from sliding

00:29:58.188 --> 00:30:01.200
On&nbsp;the top, we have a chamfered handle.

00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:03.813
So, we have 11 more of these to make...

00:30:03.813 --> 00:30:06.300
We're&nbsp;gonna get the team involved, and knock them out!

00:30:39.271 --> 00:30:39.771
Okay!

00:30:39.771 --> 00:30:42.416
So, at this point, we've finished all&nbsp;12 of the lids!

00:30:42.416 --> 00:30:46.500
They've been sanded, they've been oiled,
and now they're ready&nbsp;to be taken to their home forever.

00:30:50.880 --> 00:30:52.140
Let's see if they fit!

00:30:54.660 --> 00:30:55.440
They fit!

00:31:01.380 --> 00:31:03.776
- This is the second week into the new poop&nbsp;system.

00:31:03.776 --> 00:31:06.180
We only have four buckets!

00:31:10.560 --> 00:31:13.000
We open up what we have covered&nbsp;last week...

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:14.822
We put the new poop in...

00:31:14.822 --> 00:31:17.282
It connects the last week's poop...

00:31:17.282 --> 00:31:18.720
And&nbsp;then, we will cover it again, of course!

00:31:21.835 --> 00:31:23.455
- Oh! There it is!

00:31:25.140 --> 00:31:26.184
You're scared?

00:31:26.184 --> 00:31:28.500
Yes! Very much!

00:31:30.900 --> 00:31:33.418
- It doesn't look that bad!

00:31:34.271 --> 00:31:36.013
Last one!

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:51.060
- We had a beat going.

00:31:55.320 --> 00:31:57.561
What, Julie?

00:31:57.561 --> 00:31:58.440
- I'm seeing something moving!

00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:02.284
Yeah, that happens...

00:32:02.284 --> 00:32:03.900
We also saw that last time.

00:32:07.020 --> 00:32:10.200
Now that we put the poured the&nbsp;poop in, we cover it again.

00:32:14.644 --> 00:32:15.817
- It looks like it's finished, no?

00:32:15.817 --> 00:32:16.653
Yeah!

00:32:16.653 --> 00:32:17.525
- Ready for another week!

00:32:17.525 --> 00:32:19.088
We covered the poop.

00:32:19.088 --> 00:32:24.240
So, now that our poop system is running,
 we can&nbsp;go back to the building of the toilet.

00:32:26.940 --> 00:32:32.262
Today, I'm going to be working on the last&nbsp;
missing part of the toilet

00:32:32.262 --> 00:32:33.864
We'll build a little sink area.

00:32:33.864 --> 00:32:39.982
Last week, I saw this nice piece&nbsp;of red cedar at the sawmill.

00:32:39.982 --> 00:32:45.402
So, my idea is to cut a straight line in the back,
 which is&nbsp;going to be the back of the sink.

00:32:45.402 --> 00:32:55.156
Leave the front live edge, and then try 
and cut two 45-degree-angles here and here.

00:32:55.156 --> 00:32:57.960
To fold the two pieces.

00:33:25.140 --> 00:33:29.880
I ran into a bit of a problem&nbsp;here:
my blade isn't deep enough...

00:33:30.780 --> 00:33:33.161
So, this is as far as it goes.

00:33:33.161 --> 00:33:36.540
I think&nbsp;I'm going to have to flip the piece.

00:33:49.860 --> 00:33:51.529
just finished the cuts!

00:33:51.529 --> 00:33:53.445
pretty happy with it!

00:33:53.445 --> 00:33:58.200
I love the book match we have right now here from the grain.

00:33:58.200 --> 00:33:58.980
So cool!

00:34:42.540 --> 00:34:43.860
I think it looks pretty cool!

00:35:00.530 --> 00:35:03.875
What? A second toilet?

00:35:06.660 --> 00:35:10.140
It's good, but let's check it with a big guy!

00:35:12.960 --> 00:35:13.920
- It works!

00:35:24.480 --> 00:35:25.304
Okay

00:35:25.304 --> 00:35:28.440
So, this is the light we&nbsp;have been using in the old toilet.

00:35:29.700 --> 00:35:36.016
Inside it, there are four LED's on the front&nbsp;and the back.

00:35:36.016 --> 00:35:38.089
And, for the back one, we never use it.

00:35:38.089 --> 00:35:44.166
So, we took it out and put it in the old light,
 that we got from the yellow van.

00:35:44.166 --> 00:35:45.540
Let's connect them!

00:35:56.200 --> 00:36:02.320
During the building of the toilet,&nbsp;
I made the cable for the light connections.

00:36:43.080 --> 00:36:45.780
To finish everything, we filled a jerrycan with water.

00:36:57.540 --> 00:36:59.280
We filled the sawdust box.

00:37:07.860 --> 00:37:10.719
It's nice to see that everything works!

00:37:11.714 --> 00:37:13.304
How&nbsp;many do you think we can put in?

00:37:13.304 --> 00:37:14.013
- Three.

00:37:14.013 --> 00:37:16.490
Those blue buckets here?

00:37:16.490 --> 00:37:20.000
- Four of them is just gonna&nbsp;be too much,
 but three of those we can fit in.

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:21.196
Which already helps a lot!

00:37:21.534 --> 00:37:25.500
We inserted an awesome&nbsp;toilet paper holder,
 made out of mimosa!

00:37:32.040 --> 00:37:35.040
Then, we covered the area with some dirt and wood chips

00:37:50.880 --> 00:37:53.580
So, this is the inside of the toilet!

00:37:53.580 --> 00:37:56.569
It's looking&nbsp;good, with a lot of space.

00:37:56.569 --> 00:38:00.350
Here we have light that Kevin did!

00:38:00.350 --> 00:38:04.209
Here is a window for some natural&nbsp;
light and some ventilation.

00:38:04.209 --> 00:38:05.220
A precious plastic seat.

00:38:05.940 --> 00:38:06.812
Cool!

00:38:07.309 --> 00:38:13.337
Here, we have a compartment for&nbsp;
toilet paper storage and a period basket.

00:38:14.100 --> 00:38:16.830
And, here we have the storage for sawdust!

00:38:16.830 --> 00:38:18.971
We also have Dave with us always.

00:38:18.971 --> 00:38:20.760
Here we store all the sawdust!

00:38:22.140 --> 00:38:25.661
This box is connected through a hole in&nbsp;the wall.

00:38:25.661 --> 00:38:29.297
It goes to the sawdust storage for the inside part of the toilet.

00:38:29.297 --> 00:38:30.479
Here is the sink!

00:38:30.479 --> 00:38:32.809
It's&nbsp;a simple system.

00:38:32.809 --> 00:38:37.273
We just have this water container,
 which we can get some water from.

00:38:37.273 --> 00:38:44.220
When we're finished cleaning our hands,
 we can just get the water and throw&nbsp;it, or we can also water the plant.

00:38:46.020 --> 00:38:52.380
The backdoor: if we open it, there is some space
 for the poop bucket and we added some rails.

00:38:52.380 --> 00:38:56.506
Just so that is easier to fit, and here,
 we can store&nbsp;some more toilet paper also.

00:38:56.506 --> 00:38:58.309
But, the roof is not finished...

00:38:58.309 --> 00:39:02.025
We want to try our experimental roof made with cans.

00:39:02.025 --> 00:39:04.087
Here's a sample that Kevin made!

00:39:05.118 --> 00:39:07.031
Looks awesome!

00:39:07.031 --> 00:39:08.724
But, for that, we need more cans.

00:39:08.724 --> 00:39:10.685
500 in total.

00:39:10.685 --> 00:39:13.306
We will show it in another update!

00:39:13.306 --> 00:39:14.419
Subscribe to follow!

00:39:14.419 --> 00:39:17.990
We are also publishing the drawings of&nbsp;
this toilet in the research model.

00:39:17.990 --> 00:39:20.625
You can replicate it or improve it!

00:39:20.625 --> 00:39:23.374
And, this is our new&nbsp;poop area!

00:39:23.374 --> 00:39:24.720
Let's see how it goes in the long run.

00:39:26.520 --> 00:39:27.827
So, the toilet is done!

00:39:27.827 --> 00:39:31.498
I am, sorry, we are very happy&nbsp;with the result!

00:39:31.498 --> 00:39:33.485
That's it for this video!

00:39:33.485 --> 00:39:36.976
The next video is gonna be about getting some goats!

00:39:36.976 --> 00:39:37.534
I'm joking...

00:39:37.534 --> 00:39:39.024
It's gonna be about kitchen.

00:39:39.024 --> 00:39:42.820
So, if you'd like to see the video now,
 you can support us on Patreon!

00:39:42.820 --> 00:39:45.503
And, if not, we'll see you next week.

00:39:45.503 --> 00:39:47.820
Bye!

